	quest.315C6016D88D781D.quest_desc: [
		"Immune to lightning damage"
		"&6&lLightning Resistance [Unlock Codex]"
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/curios/shock_pendant.png width:50 height:80 align:left}"
		""
		"Release lightning to strike your opponent"
		"&6&lLightning Guard [Unlock Codex]"
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/curios/shock_pendant_2.png width:50 height:80 align:left}"
	]
	quest.315C6016D88D781D.quest_subtitle: "The Flash"
	quest.31893B7163684E99.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have memorized a &bConstellation&f, you'll see it light up and sparkle in the night sky among the other stars. They will often be a different color, making it easier for you to trace them with your &aAstrolabe&f."
		""
		"Using the &aAstrolabe&f, you can also search for &3Focal Points&f where a &bConstellation's&f light hits the ground. You'll know where one is by the bare patch left in the nearby grass."
		""
		"At night, you can configure the &aAstrolabe's&f marker to the right angle to reveal a column of light where the &3Focal Point&f is. Look straight at it to mark that spot in your memory."
		""
		"Human star-wizards learned to read these patterns as guides for shaping magicules, seeking through the heavens a deeper understanding of &6Veldanava&f and the order he left in the Cardinal World."
	]
	quest.31893B7163684E99.title: "&bReading the Skies"
	quest.318F8A3B3BBD8349.quest_desc: [
		"Dwarves are creatures similar to villagers that can be traded and their craftsmanship is the best in the world!"
		"Trading with them requires coins, not emeralds."
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/dwarf_village.png width:130 height:70 align:center}"
		""
		"In large city-states, you can also see dwarf magicians, and you can trade some strange things with them.&5magical tome&rOr trade it with a master magician&5wand blueprint&r"
	]
	quest.318F8A3B3BBD8349.quest_subtitle: "Find where the dwarves live."
	quest.318F8A3B3BBD8349.title: "Capital of the Dwarves"
	quest.31C0A79015BCD0A3.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.31CC7F2DE56B10CD.quest_subtitle: "A &6Brass Tunnel&r is an upgrade to the &6Andesite Tunnel&r, allowing more configurability in how to deal with items"
	quest.31CC7F2DE56B10CD.title: "Obtain Brass Tunnel"
	quest.31F3C50FFA640427.quest_subtitle: "&5Very Rare"
	quest.31F3C50FFA640427.title: "Catch Marstilus"
	quest.3207FC214E81882A.quest_subtitle: "When placed in front of the &6Encased Fan&r, &9water&r allows it to wash items"
	quest.3207FC214E81882A.title: "Obtain Water Bucket"
	quest.321ECD9F13D78465.quest_subtitle: "【Mastery】"
	quest.321ECD9F13D78465.title: "&6【Advanced】&f Obtain the Unique Skill Infinite Prison"
	quest.3228ABCCB6B932FC.title: "{translate:\"task.D4E5F6A7B8C90133.title\"}"
	quest.323F20F8AFC2C633.title: "&cMinecart with TNT"
	quest.3242CBD006ABEFF3.quest_desc: ["The Solegnolia keeps magnets at bay. Craft one to protect nearby items from magnetic effects."]
	quest.3242CBD006ABEFF3.quest_subtitle: "Keeps magnets at bay"
	quest.3242CBD006ABEFF3.title: "Solegnolia"
	quest.325BE865B5571472.title: "Kill the Sunbird - Umuwuti"
	quest.326B2F79F3A9D8D7.quest_subtitle: "Produce more than 1000 &fTrain Tracks&r with the same Mechanical Press"
	quest.326B2F79F3A9D8D7.title: "&6Track Factory"
	quest.326BB81BA22F0E4E.title: "&d&lWelcome to the Fun Section"
	quest.3286EEB38D29B8AA.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.32C1B30C5CE46F13.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.32E1EA9C678DFF9C.quest_desc: ["The center slot is where the finished item appears. The slots on either side are used to melt and store minerals during fusion."]
	quest.32E1EA9C678DFF9C.quest_subtitle: "Alas, how to refine it?"
	quest.32E1EA9C678DFF9C.title: "&6【Forging Line·Important】&r Burning Minerals, Forging Artifacts"
	quest.32FEF370F61CA35C.quest_desc: ["&8Maybe it's useless for players who have maps, but what if it's an underground dragon's lair?"]
	quest.32FEF370F61CA35C.quest_subtitle: "Looking for dragon props?"
	quest.33058894ACD9CB06.quest_desc: ["The Graveyard is where the Undertaker will bury your deceased citizens. When a citizen dies, a grave will spawn at the location of death. The Undertaker will attempt to recover the grave before it despawns. If successful, the Undertaker will return to the graveyard and attempt to revive the citizen. If the citizen cannot be revived, the Undertaker will bury them in the Graveyard. Another grave will be placed with the citizen’s name on it."]
	quest.33058894ACD9CB06.quest_subtitle: "Build a Graveyard"
	quest.330A773979CC2104.quest_subtitle: "&aA Few More Steps"
	quest.332803BFA6D1A237.quest_subtitle: "Queen of the Ice Castle"
	quest.33334EFC5EC1E3B6.quest_desc: ["It is immune to all conventional attacks and status effects. If you hit it normally, it will basically not lose any blood."]
	quest.33334EFC5EC1E3B6.quest_subtitle: "What You Need to Know"
	quest.33722877653074AA.quest_subtitle: "&dCulinary Ordeal"
	quest.337BA8FE36665B99.quest_subtitle: "A flexible diode that can output precisely timed redstone pulses according to a configured sequence"
	quest.337BA8FE36665B99.title: "&cSequenced Pulse Generator"
	quest.337C56118E98F19E.title: "{translate:\"task.8B9C0D1E2F3A4568.title\"}"
	quest.338C386DD712406B.quest_subtitle: "&aA Few More Steps"
	quest.33A31F36D0204245.quest_desc: [
		"It has two stages. In the first stage, all moves will be used, and the second stage only enhances the previous functions."
		"&6The skills it possesses are fire attack negation, heat negation, abnormal status negation, body strengthening and steel power."
	]
	quest.33A31F36D0204245.title: "Crusade Against the Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.33AB6B567959623B.quest_desc: ["It spawns on the second floor of the Flame Arena. Defeat it to obtain four Burning Embers.&lBurning Embers&r. Hold one and right-click the Altar of Flame to summon the Flame Demon."]
	quest.33AB6B567959623B.quest_subtitle: "Blaze's brother?"
	quest.33AB6B567959623B.title: "Kill the Burning Relic"
	quest.33AF04527684D9B5.quest_desc: [
		"Throw logs into a pool of &bLiquid Starlight&f to turn them into &aInfused Wood&f. This is one of the core crafting components for many &eAstral Sorcery&f recipes."
		""
		"The pool isn't consumed for this recipe, so one pool can convert as many logs as you want."
	]
	quest.33AF04527684D9B5.title: "&aInfused Wood"
	quest.33B3C5F33B18C4F3.title: "&eTrain Casing"
	quest.33C7424919F54C10.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lGreetings, Reincarnator. Welcome to your Second Life."
		"&fThis modpack is a modification of &aTensura Neo Otherworld&f. There may be bugs!"
		""
		"&e&lDid You Know?"
		"&b"
		"[ { \"text\": \"『You Can Force Blocks to Load』\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"7D00E143DC7B8D9E\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.33C7424919F54C10.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to your Second Life!"
	quest.3407EC8CA3F0C20F.quest_subtitle: "Ruler of the Sky"
	quest.3407EC8CA3F0C20F.title: "Scales of Charybdis"
	quest.342A1EF584823D2C.quest_desc: ["Okay this achievement is kind of a lie. It might be more analogous to “teach a man to fish”.  Regardless, the point is that if you teach your builder to make simple items that fit in a 2x2 crafting grid (like torches) they can craft the item themselves instead of asking for help."]
	quest.3452B7872FD9A598.quest_desc: ["The Worldshaper's Astrolabe is Botania's building tool. Craft one to add this terrain-shaping tool to your kit."]
	quest.3452B7872FD9A598.quest_subtitle: "Botania's building tool"
	quest.3452B7872FD9A598.title: "Worldshaper's Astrolabe"
	quest.346A98CF74B3DDCC.quest_subtitle: "&bDemanding Dish"
	quest.346B9FB4CDBA827C.quest_subtitle: "What are you stir-frying without a spatula?"
	quest.34715BD264350DDC.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.34BDEA7471099252.title: "&dMinecart with Furnace"
	quest.34C35E7555875A09.quest_subtitle: "Drops from killing Netherite Monstrosity."
	quest.34D8E3A129C8B3D9.quest_desc: [
		"&l\"Temporal Dawn\""
		"Long ago, time in the Overworld did not flow in a straight line."
		"In the old era, a group of clockmakers discovered a strange ore. Unlike iron and gold, it was not silent. It trembled softly in the night, as if hiding an invisible chime. The clockmakers called it Clockstone. They used Clockstone to build towers, engrave blueprints, and forge gears, attempting to open the gate at the end of time."
		""
		"..."
		""
		"But the first people who entered Temporal Dawn never returned. After they crossed through, the portal became one-way. The ancient clockmakers realized that what they had opened was not a treasure vault, but a prison sealed shut by time..."
	]
	quest.34D8E3A129C8B3D9.quest_subtitle: "Disordered Space-Time"
	quest.34FF589B697722F3.quest_subtitle: "It's just a &6Seat&r, nothing more, nothing less. But if you're in a moving contraption, you might as well glue it to the contraption so you can sit and move along with it"
	quest.34FF589B697722F3.title: "Seat"
	quest.351D8C60DBC88BF8.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have 200,000 EP and a Demon Lord Seed, you can start collecting &#FF6F01souls&r by killing various high-EP mobs."
		"For example, killing:"
		"Charybdis grants &#B90E74800 souls&r"
		"Hinata grants &#B90E74518 souls"
		"An Elemental Colossus (first time) grants &#B90E74175 souls"
		"A Metal Slime grants &#B90E74150 souls"
		"The Orc Disaster grants &#B90E74125 souls"
		"A Greater Demon grants &#B90E7470 souls"
		""
		"Of course, any other mob can also grant souls, provided it has EP."
		"&4Warning: Dying causes you to lose 5% of your souls!&r"
	]
	quest.35289058F397A21C.title: "&6【Main Story】&r EP Reaches 1.8 Million"
	quest.3550C890B3367EA4.quest_subtitle: "&bDemanding Dish"
	quest.35606BC47E5DCBCF.quest_subtitle: "Kill without taking damage."
	quest.3560772906E36142.quest_desc: [
		"&3Celestial Crystals&f are upgraded versions of &2Rock Crystals&f, starting off with better stats and with better growth potential."
		""
		"Drop &aStardust&f and a &3Crystal&f together into a pool of &bLiquid Starlight&f. After the pool is consumed, it leaves behind a small &3Celestial Crystal Cluster&f."
		""
		"It grows on its own under open sky, faster at night, and faster still on &aStarmetal Ore&f, though that can turn the ore back into iron. Wait until it's fully grown and shimmering before breaking it with a pickaxe."
	]
	quest.3560772906E36142.title: "&3Celestial Crystal"
	quest.356481588F239F15.title: "&9Fan Haunting Catalyst"
	quest.3568CFD26A402E3E.quest_subtitle: "&6Ultima's Table"
	quest.3579EE70549D6DBF.quest_subtitle: "An upgraded version of the &6Copper Diving Helmet&r"
	quest.3579EE70549D6DBF.title: "Obtain Netherite Diving Helmet"
	quest.35AEBB19E643C7F7.quest_desc: [
		"A &2Focus Relay&f holds one item above it, and an altar surrounded by relays will use their items during a craft."
		""
		"Right-click a relay with an item to place it, and Right-click with an empty hand to take it back."
		""
		"Relays don't need linking, only correct placement, so put them exactly where the &bTome's&f structure page shows."
		""
		"The next altar needs a ring made up of eight &2Relays&f."
	]
	quest.35AEBB19E643C7F7.title: "&2Focus Relay"
	quest.35C8929631187831.quest_subtitle: "A &6Packager&r will pack items from the connected inventory into a package when given &credstone&r power"
	quest.35C8929631187831.title: "Obtain Packager"
	quest.35FDAB9FED24F4C5.quest_desc: ["A Mana Splitter divides incoming mana among adjacent Mana Pools. Use one to distribute a flower's output across several storage pools."]
	quest.35FDAB9FED24F4C5.title: "Mana Splitter"
	quest.360E9E02A494217C.quest_subtitle: "Build Barracks Tower Inside the Barracks"
	quest.3619EEA1236FDB0F.quest_subtitle: "Crash into another &bTrain&r while driving backwards"
	quest.3619EEA1236FDB0F.title: "Blind Spot"
	quest.362F033FC7A21D59.quest_desc: [
		"For now, you can only encounter her in the wild. Structures will be added in a future update."
		"Her abilities are mainly physical, but watch out for her ultimate move!"
		""
		"&#FF5E30This boss is still a work in progress.&r"
	]
	quest.362F033FC7A21D59.quest_subtitle: "Don't Be So Naughty"
	quest.362F033FC7A21D59.title: "Are You One-Punch Man?"
	quest.36872A791869885E.quest_subtitle: "The Best Choice for Making Weapons and Equipment"
	quest.36872A791869885E.title: "Stronger Than Netherite!"
	quest.36B943AC67817D08.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.36BA327364892B26.quest_subtitle: "&2Uncommon"
	quest.36BA327364892B26.title: "Catch Blowfish"
	quest.37090F5115C27AAD.quest_desc: ["Sparks move mana between pools without a Mana Spreader. Place them on the pools you want to connect; Spark Augments can guide or filter the transfer."]
	quest.37090F5115C27AAD.title: "Sparks"
	quest.37220E036887A3FD.title: "Small Lesser Taratect"
	quest.373CBF2E3F0D7C29.quest_subtitle: "&5Very Rare"
	quest.373CBF2E3F0D7C29.title: "Catch Aquathorn"
	quest.3746CA2ADED125A1.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.376F28B8624324AC.quest_subtitle: "An &cAnalog Lever&r can be set to output any redstone level. It's basically an upgraded version of the basic lever"
	quest.376F28B8624324AC.title: "Obtain Analog Lever"
	quest.3793BC9A3109DA3E.quest_desc: [
		"A book about this plant can be found. Hippokute Grass grows throughout the world.&5It is highly sensitive to Magicules&r, so seeds are more likely to appear where Magicule concentrations are higher."
		""
		"How to use: Plant a&2Hippokute Seed&r in grass, dirt, or farmland."
		"{image:tensura:item/hipokute_seeds width:20 height:20 align:center}"
		"&lRandom Growth Mechanics:&r"
		""
		"● In the Overworld, there is a&610% chance every 0.05 seconds&r that the seed will grow into Hippokute Grass."
		""
		"● &6If planted in the Nether, the chance increases to 25%!&r"
		""
		"● Otherwise, there is a&690% chance&r the seed will grow into regular wheat. In the Nether, regular wheat has a 75% chance to grow."
		"{image:tensura:item/hipokute_grass width:20 height:20 align:center}"
		"● When the plant reaches the \"grass\" stage, there is a&650% chance&r it will become&2&lHippokute Grass&r."
		""
		"{image:tensura:item/hipokute_flower width:20 height:20 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3793BC9A3109DA3E.quest_subtitle: "Where can I find this special seed?"
	quest.3793BC9A3109DA3E.title: "&6[Medicine Refining Branch]&r Obtain Hippokute Seed"
	quest.379A02354D2E8B3C.quest_subtitle: "Kill bosses in order."
	quest.37B21D9B564CCEBA.quest_desc: [
		"Where to use this mineral to make weapons and equipment is a wise choice, but its rarity is no less than that of ancient wreckage."
		"If you are going to mine this mineral, you will need to prepare a handful&6Next alloy pickaxe&r, otherwise you won’t be able to dig it out at all!"
		""
		"Of course, you can also get 1 to 6 metal slimes by killing them, but can you find them and keep up with them?&6It has physical attack resistance and regeneration capabilities&r"
	]
	quest.37B21D9B564CCEBA.quest_subtitle: "Crystal filled with Magicule..."
	quest.37B21D9B564CCEBA.title: "&6【Forging Line·Important】&r Dig for Rare Minerals"
	quest.37BE190EE466D697.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade the Town Hall to Level 5"
	quest.37C4A1ED1E0E1822.title: "Lesser Taratect"
	quest.37E43341FA234E84.quest_desc: [
		"The Flower Shop is where your Florist will grow flowers for your colony, if given compost and an axe. "
		""
		"One important factor to know is that the flower shop has a daily flower limit based on the hut level. Level 1 has a daily max of 4, level 2 has 8. At level 5 it’s daily max is 20. "
	]
	quest.37E43341FA234E84.quest_subtitle: "Build a Flower Shop"
	quest.37E707CBDB2CDDCD.title: "{translate:\"task.B2C3D4E5F6A70901.title\"}"
	quest.37F3C6EA2B70D83A.quest_subtitle: "&6Connectors&r insert and extract energy from blocks, while &6Wires&r are used to link connectors"
	quest.37F3C6EA2B70D83A.title: "Obtain Connector"
	quest.380C4417E7F958A6.quest_desc: [
		"Set an &3Attuned Crystal&f into a lattice to make a &dStarlight Focus Crystal&f, a starlight source. It keeps the stats of the &3Crystal&f inside it, and size and cut decide how much starlight it produces."
		""
		"It has to be placed in the column of a &3Focal Point&f that matches its &bConstellation&f. Once set up, it shows a fan of colored light, makes the &3Focal Point's&f beam visible without an &aAstrolabe&f, and flight in an area around it."
		""
		"It only produces starlight at night while its &bConstellation&f is in the sky."
	]
	quest.380C4417E7F958A6.title: "&dStarlight Focus Crystal"
	quest.381650201BD5521E.quest_desc: [
		"Possess a weakened physical body to enter a whole new world."
		"How to use:"
		"&lActive Skill&r If used while in a possession state, leaves the body (unless it is the original body, it will disappear after 5 minutes to avoid lag) and its inherent Skills, and transforms the player into spirit form. In spirit form, if the player can possess the target: [Ineffective against targets with psychic attack immunity]"
		""
		"&l- Non-player monsters: &r"
		"Health below 10%, spiritual health below 10%, or maximum EP less than 25% (relative to the user) - If the target has spiritual attack resistance, drops to 5% health, 5% spirit health, or 12.5% EP."
		""
		"&l- Player:&r Requires 2 of the 3 optional conditions above. If possessed, the target player enters spirit form, and without the [Possession] skill will eventually die."
		"When possessing the target, the user returns to physical form with the target's physical attributes and skills."
		""
		"&lWarning: When using this skill, held items and armor will remain on the old body.&r"
		""
		"&lFriendly reminder:&r Access your inventory and retrieve these items from the old body."
		"When switching bodies via Possession, only status effects with the \"spiritual affected\" tag are transferred; other regular status effects will not be transferred with the soul."
	]
	quest.381650201BD5521E.quest_subtitle: "Your Inner Skill"
	quest.381B864E35C59018.title: "{translate:\"task.E5F6A7B8C9D01244.title\"}"
	quest.38885CD90AF0F1E8.quest_desc: [
		"These five runes are the first set needed to progress toward Terrasteel. Further runes open more recipes and devices."
		""
		"Botania's flora and mana-powered tools branch in many directions from here. Follow the Lexica Botania and pursue the optional paths that suit your needs."
	]
	quest.38885CD90AF0F1E8.title: "The Runes"
	quest.38BE2F3E7F5B1C5F.quest_desc: "Right-click the portal frame to activate it, then use the Time Hourglass to reactivate the portal"
	quest.38BE2F3E7F5B1C5F.quest_subtitle: "Activate the portal back."
	quest.38C6CA73A1BFB0CF.title: "&eCandy Cane Pickaxe"
	quest.391FA9B8D6B130A7.quest_desc: ["There are 3 main ways of getting &2Nuggets of Experiences&r: &6Crushing Wheels&r, &bdropped by slain Mobs&r or &dBottles of Experience&r."]
	quest.391FA9B8D6B130A7.quest_subtitle: "Don't right click it or you'll absorb it all"
	quest.391FA9B8D6B130A7.title: "&2Nuggets of Experience"
	quest.393CDA23EE2BA33B.quest_subtitle: "&aA Few More Steps"
	quest.39472502FF781B84.quest_subtitle: "Find the cave within [Choose a route; solo players can challenge them all]."
	quest.395C303A0B300171.quest_desc: "&6Has a 1% chance to drop when harvesting fully grown crops.&r While possessing Shub-Niggurath, Lord of Harvest, consume 10 of these to lock this Ultimate Skill through the “Lock” screen, preventing it from being lost upon reincarnation."
	quest.395C303A0B300171.quest_subtitle: "Preserve This Skill"
	quest.398A8349245D65C4.quest_subtitle: "&bDemanding Dish"
