		"Sneak + Right-click a blank &aScroll of Written Expertise&f to record everything you've learned so you can share it with friends."
		""
		"Anyone else can Right-click it to learn your &bConstellations&f, &3Focal Points&f and progress."
	]
	quest.442EB58BFF66C799.title: "&aScroll of Written Expertise"
	quest.443889DBF90B8B8F.quest_subtitle: "Rest easy, young chef. You have earned this prize."
	quest.443889DBF90B8B8F.title: "&6They Whom Food Eternally Loves"
	quest.445212E6651B7746.title: "Obtain Candy Cane Block"
	quest.4454735A12F6DC87.quest_desc: [
		"It can spawn in Overworld structures, including Japanese-style buildings. Master Cartographer Villagers may offer a map to its structure, and it can also spawn in the wild."
		""
		"&8Neutral to all creatures unless attacked&r"
		"This is Rimuru's form during the Great Oni War, possessing the two unique Skills of Predator and Great Sage."
		""
		"&lBOSS stage explanation:&r"
		""
		"&lFirst Stage&r"
		"&6-Has a 20% chance to dodge physical attacks and teleports to the target when dodging."
		"&6-Can swallow arrows and other projectiles."
		"&6-Skills available: water blade, ice gun, web bullets, breath (random paralysis/poison/black fire)."
		"&6-Restore 5 health points + 20 soul health points per second."
		"&6-Enters the second phase when his HP falls below 50% or drops below 1,000.&r"
		""
		"&lSecond stage (armored form)&r"
		"&6-When entering this stage, Rimuru will fully restore health and soul health, and clear all negative effects."
		"&6-Equip a full armored dragon suit and armored dragon gauntlet."
		"&6-Summon 4 clones to assist in the battle (the clones have 10% of the main body's EP)."
		"&6-His passive regeneration increases to 15 health points and 60 soul health points per second."
		"&6-In this stage, Rimuru will use all the Skills in the first stage, and additionally cast: Hellfire, Black Thunder, and Coercion."
		""
		"&6Rimuru respawns 40 minutes after being defeated."
	]
	quest.4454735A12F6DC87.quest_subtitle: "I want to challenge you."
	quest.4454735A12F6DC87.title: "Are You Rimuru?"
	quest.4488E4793D485C08.quest_subtitle: "Defeat a Giant Miner"
	quest.44EAB4E7B89294C3.quest_subtitle: "&2Uncommon"
	quest.44EAB4E7B89294C3.title: "Catch Judgment Fish"
	quest.44F3DD36CE3B6D30.quest_desc: [
		"&dStardew&f is a flask filled from a cauldron of water. Bind a lumen to it the same way you bind gear, and drinking it gives that aspect's effect:"
		""
		"- &bAevitas&f gives Regeneration"
		"- &3Armara&f gives Resistance"
		"- &bDiscidia&f gives Strength"
		"- &3Evorsio&f gives Haste"
		"- &bVicio&f gives Speed"
		""
		"Unlike gear, a flask keeps every binding you give it, so the effects stack. It only holds a few drinks before it needs to be refilled and bound again."
	]
	quest.44F3DD36CE3B6D30.title: "&dStardew"
	quest.450B76DAD9BD8ED6.quest_subtitle: "&9Rare"
	quest.450B76DAD9BD8ED6.title: "Catch Red 40"
