	quest.6F7A8B9C0D1E2345.title: "{translate:\"task.6F7A8B9C0D1E2346.title\"}"
	quest.6F7B8AD6377B3621.quest_subtitle: "A &6Mechanical Roller&r lets you clear blocks in front and pave with desired blocks underneath the tracks while riding a train"
	quest.6F7B8AD6377B3621.title: "Obtain Mechanical Roller"
	quest.6F998D330698620F.title: "Obtain Cocoa Butter"
	quest.6FADE50D16AE827B.quest_subtitle: "&aA Few More Steps"
	quest.6FC262DD2B5C2847.quest_desc: [
		"&#FFED54Hyperlink:&r"
		"[ { \"text\": \"How Artifacts Work\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"4DB740093C0BA804\" } } ] "
		""
		"Default Effects"
		"&5Effect 1: Silent Strike"
		"Attacking from behind, or while the target is not focused on the wearer, increases the damage of the next attack. Has a 30-second cooldown."
		"&5Effect 2: Armor Exploitation"
		"Increases critical-hit rate based on the target's Armor."
		"For every 5 Armor the target has, the wearer's critical-hit rate against that target increases."
		"&5Effect 3: Shadow Slash Mode"
		"Adds Shadow Slash Mode to Shadow Striker."
		"When used, Shadow Slash teleports the wearer behind the target they are facing and immediately attacks."
		"The attack deals critical damage with an additional Critical Damage bonus. It also applies a Resistance reduction effect on hit."
		""
		"Refinement Bonuses"
		"Silent Strike Scaling"
		"Each refinement increases Silent Strike's damage bonus by an additional 5%."
		"Maximum: At +3 refinement, Silent Strike can deal up to 65% increased damage."
		"Armor Exploitation Scaling"
		"Each refinement increases the critical-hit rate gained for every 5 Armor."
		"Maximum: At +3 refinement, Armor Exploitation can provide up to 0.5% critical-hit rate per 5 Armor."
		"Shadow Slash Mode Scaling"
		"Each refinement increases Shadow Slash Mode's Critical Damage bonus by an additional +5."
		"Maximum: At +3 refinement, Shadow Slash Mode can provide up to +50 Critical Damage."
	]
	quest.6FC262DD2B5C2847.title: "&6【Artifact】&f Grade 1 Ancient Artifact"
	quest.6FD71D5F8A7AE472.quest_desc: ["You can only obtain this material from a dragon that has not yet been reduced to a skeleton."]
	quest.6FD71D5F8A7AE472.quest_subtitle: "Dragon Heart, Eat Immortality"
	quest.6FD71D5F8A7AE472.title: "Obtain the Dragon Heart"
	quest.6FDBD38851854574.title: "&6[Advanced]&f Obtain the Unique Skill Gluttony"
	quest.6FEC40832C92107A.quest_subtitle: "&7Simple Fare"
	quest.6FFEE47366330B47.quest_subtitle: "&dCulinary Ordeal"
	quest.7003D050CAD2307C.title: "Redstone + Create"
	quest.70251D1E0D33F89A.quest_subtitle: "&7Common"
	quest.70251D1E0D33F89A.title: "Catch Pike"
	quest.7063E2EA02FBC5EA.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike the &eMagic Engine&r, the &b&lMagicule Repelling Brazier&r doesn't reduce the amount of magicules in an area. Instead, one could say it actually makes them more pronounced. But it does this without injecting more magicules, and instead uses a ritual to stir up the bonds between particles in the air. Sort of like a humidifier, but for ambient magic particles."
		""
		"This heightened density doesn't give much issue to those with strong souls, but animals and creatures with lots of magicules find the space uncomfortable for an entirely different reason from the Magic Engine. Instead of feeling weak and breathless, the amount of energy reacting with their bodies borders on excessive, causing their inner magicules to perform an act not too far off from the concept of hyperventilating."
		""
		"Due to the restriction of needing a high &6Existence Value&f to feel the negative effects of this device, farm creatures, fish, and even domesticated animals like cats and dogs have no issue living in a region protected by a Magicule Repelling Brazier."
	]
	quest.7063E2EA02FBC5EA.quest_subtitle: "When the Magic Engine isn't enough."
	quest.7063E2EA02FBC5EA.title: "Another: Magicule Repelling Brazier"
	quest.70667601EB2E48E3.quest_subtitle: "&2Uncommon"
	quest.70667601EB2E48E3.title: "Catch Boxfish"
	quest.7071E6CEA90C4164.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apotheosis&r expands equipment progression through &eAffixes&r: weapons and armor can gain rarity-ranked modifiers that improve attributes, add combat effects, or grant unusual abilities."
		""
		"&bGems&r provide specialized bonuses when fitted into equipment with &bSockets&r, while reforging and augmenting let you shape or strengthen an item's Affixes."
		""
		"In this world, progression is not paced by climbing through &cWorld Tiers&r. That global tier ladder is unavailable, but the equipment systems and their loot remain available."
		""
		"Instead, an ordinary non-boss creature's &dExistence Points (EP)&r determine its chance to become an &6Apothic Invader&r, and also inform the strength of the gear it receives. Some Apothic foes can also wield &bSkills&r."
	]
	quest.7071E6CEA90C4164.title: "&6What Is Apotheosis?"
	quest.7072291CC468F0EA.quest_desc: [
		"How to obtain: Have EP."
		""
		"&l[Passive - Toggle]:&r"
		"If a creature begins attacking the user, a bell sound plays for the user."
	]
	quest.7072291CC468F0EA.quest_subtitle: "Sense Hostile Intent?"
	quest.7072291CC468F0EA.title: "&6【Tips】&r Obtain and Master 【Danger Sense】"
