	quest.7B57FB93AA91033C.quest_subtitle: "Probability of Dropping"
	quest.7B5E2CD676A1A1C4.quest_desc: ["The Baker will craft bread dough, cookie dough, cake dough, and raw pumpkin pie, then bake these in a furnace to create bread, cookies, cakes, and pumpkin pies. They will only do this upon request, whether from the Cook, the postbox, or as a minimum stock in the Warehouse."]
	quest.7B5E2CD676A1A1C4.quest_subtitle: "Build a Bakery"
	quest.7B68B4B4AF7B8DA8.quest_subtitle: "&bDemanding Dish"
	quest.7B94E2CB1A399EA7.quest_subtitle: "Choose this route to craft talismans."
	quest.7BC23E4A4F041C68.quest_desc: [
		"&2Sooty Marble&f is the floor every big structure from here on stands on."
		""
		"The next altar alone sits on a five by five slab of it. Make more than you think you need."
	]
	quest.7BC23E4A4F041C68.title: "&2Sooty Marble"
	quest.7BD3A28C97D7CA72.title: "&6【Main Story】&r EP Reaches 400,000"
	quest.7C0112271677EE1D.quest_desc: [
		"1. Defeat the Ender Dragon"
		"2. Master either [Wind Manipulation] or [Wind Domination]"
		"3. Have 400,000 Magicule"
		""
		"In multiplayer, only one player may own this skill. To remove this restriction, use /gamerule VeldoraTrulgUnique false"
	]
	quest.7C0112271677EE1D.quest_subtitle: "Requirements ↓"
	quest.7C0112271677EE1D.title: "&6[Advanced]&f Ultimate Skill Veldora, Lord of Storm"
	quest.7C26D6CEC3139342.quest_subtitle: "A &6Mechanical Bearing&r allows for contraptions that rotate around a point in space, particularly useful for farms"
	quest.7C26D6CEC3139342.title: "Obtain Mechanical Bearing"
	quest.7C35B39DA62BA26F.quest_desc: [
		"The final altar upgrade needs 200 of all five basic lumen, delivered over a lumen network, &bArmara&f starlight linked from a &dStarlight Focus Crystal&f, powders and &aStardust&f on the ground, and &bLiquid Starlight&f from &3Containment Chalices&f."
		""
		"It also needs an &bArmara&f focus in the slot, which is consumed."
		""
		"The structure expands again with another ring of marble and four low pillars at the corners, as the &bTome's&f structure page shows. When it's done, the table becomes the &6Iridescent Crafting Altar&f."
	]
	quest.7C35B39DA62BA26F.quest_subtitle: "Unlocks Stellar Filaments and Artifact Enhancement"
	quest.7C35B39DA62BA26F.title: "&6Iridescent Crafting Altar"
	quest.7C50408E8C98AD23.quest_subtitle: "A device that produces immense stress when powered, halting the network by overstressing it."
	quest.7C50408E8C98AD23.title: "&6Brake"
	quest.7CAE60C40150CCBE.quest_subtitle: "You need to become a Demon Lord [See Main Story for details]."
	quest.7CB64CBAFF5C5F07.quest_desc: ["Marimorphosis changes the blocks around it into decorative stone variants. Its transformations account for several of the Petal Apothecary designs."]
	quest.7CB64CBAFF5C5F07.quest_subtitle: "Creates decorative stone variants"
	quest.7CB64CBAFF5C5F07.title: "Marimorphosis"
	quest.7CD7FD7FA288E4E6.quest_desc: [
		"Find Orc and you're halfway there!"
		""
		"&lThey are usually found in deserts and you can easily encounter them in the desert&r"
	]
	quest.7CD7FD7FA288E4E6.quest_subtitle: "Is there such a creature in the endless desert?"
	quest.7CD8CFC2880EF3AF.quest_desc: [
		"The Petal Apothecary is Botania's first crafting station. Use it to combine petals and other ingredients into flowers."
		""
		"This objective tracks the default apothecary; the other stone variants serve the same purpose."
	]
	quest.7CD8CFC2880EF3AF.title: "The Petal Apothecary"
	quest.7D000AE461BC6886.quest_desc: [
		"To choose an evolution, click the text to the right of your character model (shown in the red box). The next screen shows the evolution goal on the right and its requirements in the lower-right corner.&lIf there are many requirements, scroll down with your mouse wheel so you don't miss any."
		""
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/personal_panel_3.png width:80 height:80 align:center}"
		"The current conditions are divided into the following categories:"
		""
		"1. Obtain EP"
		"&6You gain EP by killing monsters. Normally, you receive 3% of the defeated monster's EP."
		"&r"
		"2. Consume [item]"
		"&6Most items must be eaten by right-clicking. If an item cannot be eaten directly, use the Absorption and Dissolution Skill to absorb it, then press the Skill key.&r"
		""
		"3. Kill the leader/Boss"
		"&6Any Boss counts, but each Boss can only be counted once.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"4. Get an elf"
		"&6You need to go to the Elf Maze Tree to get any elemental elf.&r"
		""
		"5. Become [True Demon Lord/True Hero]"
		"&5True Demon Lord evolution requirements"
		"&r0. Be a Demon or Chaos and possess a Demon Lord Seed."
		"1. Obtain 10,000 souls (2,000 EP = 1 soul). Reach 200,000 EP, then kill creatures to collect souls. You automatically receive the Demon Lord Seed at 200,000 EP."
		"2. Click the Awakening button on the left side of the race interface."
		"3. These requirements apply only to Demon Lord Seeds."
		"If the evolution button is not displayed after meeting the conditions, you can enter the command to evolve: /evolve demonlord"
		"&6True Brave Evolution Conditions Required"
		"&r0. Be a Creature or Chaos."
		"1. Contract with six high-level elves to obtain a Hero's Egg."
		"2. Have a Hero's Egg and at least 400,000 EP. While fighting Hinata or the Great Demon Whirlpool, reduce your health to 20% or less to become a True Hero. Alternatively, use the Hero Scroll obtained from the Main Story quest; a Hero's Egg is still required."
		""
		"6. Proficient [Skill]"
		"&6Learn and use this Skill until you become proficient.&r (This requirement is uncommon.)"
		""
		"7. Have a name"
		"&61. Press Shift+N and enable Soul Eater naming (set it to True).&r"
		"&62. Kill 1,000 humans (such as witches, villagers, Pillagers, or aliens), or complete 25 Pillager raids."
		"&63. Once you meet the requirements, the soul will be named automatically."
		"&6Note: Disabling naming does not reset your kill count. Dying resets it."
		"&6Command: [/tensura get awakening [TAB to complete your name] humanKill]"
	]
	quest.7D000AE461BC6886.title: "Race and Evolution"
	quest.7D00E143DC7B8D9E.quest_desc: [
		"The first step is to open the backpack with the E key and see the \"green map\" icon in the upper left corner."
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/chunk_map.png width:130 height:130 align:center}"
		"Click on it, then find the block you want to force load, left-click once, then SHIFT+left-click and click on it again to force-load the block, and right-click to remove the declared block (including removing forced loading)"
	]
	quest.7D00E143DC7B8D9E.quest_subtitle: "Loading chunks!"
	quest.7D00E143DC7B8D9E.title: "How to Force-Load Chunks"
	quest.7D10BFE6E3112094.title: "{translate:\"task.C3D4E5F6A7B80122.title\"}"
	quest.7D20EAB7E4E34B45.title: "&6Minecart with Chest"
	quest.7D3489901AA47547.quest_desc: [
		"The Town Hall is the central building in your colony. It provides lots of helpful information about your colony such as citizen stats, open work orders, citizen happiness, allies and more. "
		""
		"The settings tab should be a first stop for any new colonist as it contains options for hiring mode, housing assignment mode, and options to allow kids to be born. Also, this is where you can customize your colony flag. Your flag will appear on guard towers and guard shields. "
	]
	quest.7D3489901AA47547.quest_subtitle: "Build the Town Hall"
	quest.7D37D1F479745B3C.quest_subtitle: "Better than a diamond set!"
	quest.7D37D1F479745B3C.title: "Armored Dragon Suit"
	quest.7D39219C9308EF99.quest_desc: [
		"After defeating the Ender Dragon, this flower will grow on the End islands. Throw an Eye of Ender near a Rose of Oblivion to convert it into a large amount of Aura. The Rose of Oblivion can be grown in the Overworld using End Stone!"
		""
		"Finally, take some bottles to the End and collect some Aura."
	]
